00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:28.190
How are you doing?

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:29.350
What have you been up to?

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:29.950
Oh, my god.

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:34.530
Has it been?

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:37.530
It's been a week, man.

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:39.170
I will tell you.

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:49.160
So I am the primary leader for a really important initiative.

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:54.740
And because it's so important,

00:01:54.740 --> 00:02:01.170
I'm being drawn into progress check meeting, status report

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:02.170
meeting.

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:08.100
I swear to god, half of the meeting I did on Thursday

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:12.700
was me just saying the same thing over and over again

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.660
to a different crowd.

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:18.180
Because they demand their personal attention, I guess.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:20.300
I'm like, why can't we just figure out

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:21.460
how to do this proactively?

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:23.580
And I can tell all 20 of you at the same time.

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:31.820
It's partly to do with the organizational dynamics.

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:35.890
But none of that's the important stuff.

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:40.170
The important stuff is I can absolutely tell you,

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:44.620
beyond a shadow of a doubt, I am an introvert.

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:48.620
Because I have gone home every day this week,

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:51.300
just drained to the max.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:56.780
Too much people time.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:58.800
I know how it feels.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:00.700
I know you do.

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:04.340
Because we share the same letters.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:05.380
We do share letters.

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:07.780
And yeah, I get a little fried.

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:09.900
So I'm working on it.

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:10.780
Actually, it depends.

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:14.620
So as you know, if you go back like a year or two

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:17.700
in our podcast, I talked a little bit about Lincioni's

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:19.460
working geniuses.

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:26.180
And I think Meyers-Briggs and the Lincioni horoscopes

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:27.540
work well together.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:31.100
Because I'm a discerner and a galvanizer.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:34.460
I ask questions and then ask a lot of questions

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:36.580
and then get people around doing stuff.

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:40.110
I can do that stuff.

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:43.220
And it takes, even with people, it

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:45.500
takes less energy than what I'm doing.

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:49.380
If I'm in a meeting of status or all we're doing

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:52.220
is thinking about what's next and doing

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:54.260
a lot of brainstorming, I can do those things.

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:56.580
But those things take more energy out of me

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:57.860
than just being in a meeting where

00:03:57.860 --> 00:03:59.660
I get to ask lots of questions

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:02.020
and make sure I understand new stuff

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:05.350
and then get people around doing something new.

00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:06.830
I like the new.

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:08.950
I can brainstorm all day long.

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:10.630
If someone asks me my opinion.

00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:12.150
You're probably a wonder inventor.

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:13.430
We did your thing once, right?

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:16.950
Yeah.

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:19.390
I don't remember the other horoscopy thing.

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:29.490
But brainstorming, inspiring strategy.

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:31.930
We should be heading in this direction.

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:35.060
I can do that all day long.

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:44.820
But what's the ETA for blah, blah, blah, blah, blah?

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:47.820
I'm just like, just shoot me.

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:53.950
There's not enough hours remaining in the day

00:04:53.950 --> 00:04:55.670
for me to catch up on the energy.

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:00.990
It's important work.

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:05.200
It's important to get the clarity.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:09.040
But I do feel like there's been a time this week

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:10.760
where I was involved in a meeting

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:15.340
and I could have just solved the question faster

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:18.580
than empathizing with their worries

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:24.030
that I wasn't going to solve it.

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:24.510
All right.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.720
It's a flaw with me.

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:33.830
And I will absolutely say that.

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:37.990
I do, intrinsically, I don't like

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:39.950
my time wasted.

00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:44.390
And others don't necessarily know, right?

00:05:44.390 --> 00:05:48.510
But when I do these internal calculations,

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:50.710
I could have solved it by the time

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:54.680
instead of doing this meeting, right?

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:57.080
But there is one thing with the-

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:59.560
You know the cool thing now is you can be in a meeting.

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:00.800
I'm going to interrupt for real quick here.

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:03.040
I just thought you could be in a meeting where people

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:05.280
are debating over like, what should we do this,

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:06.520
or this, or this, or this?

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:07.960
And with the help of AI, you could probably

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:12.400
just write the whole solution before they actually

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:13.520
reach a conclusion.

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:15.720
Yeah, it's interesting.

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:24.220
I have found, for me, the problem with meetings now,

00:06:24.220 --> 00:06:27.500
and I don't know when it changed.

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:34.730
If you remember, certainly, you left Microsoft

00:06:34.730 --> 00:06:36.730
before COVID, right?

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:37.410
I did.

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:38.250
Most certainly.

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:39.490
I did, yes.

00:06:39.490 --> 00:06:40.930
Yes, OK.

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:42.650
So standard practice in meetings,

00:06:42.650 --> 00:06:44.730
everyone go to the meetings, have their laptop

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:46.650
and do their other work, right,

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:49.130
while pretending to listen to whatever the thing is.

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:58.490
But somehow, my pattern has changed on that one,

00:06:58.490 --> 00:07:03.420
and I am just an avid law of two feet.

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:08.020
And so I'm sitting there, and I'm either contributing

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:09.820
or I'm learning.

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:13.900
And if it's a topic that I don't care about,

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:17.980
then I'm forced to contribute.

00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:21.890
In other words, I'll either not go to the meeting

00:07:21.890 --> 00:07:23.890
now, or I'm going to go to the meeting

00:07:23.890 --> 00:07:27.150
and I'm going to be in active presence, which

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:29.950
means I can no longer kill two birds with one stone,

00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:34.270
which is pass the attendance honor roll

00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:39.220
and then get my regular work done, even with agents.

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:41.620
What I try to do is get the agent going on something

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:42.300
that's going to take a while.

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:44.980
Send the agent to the meeting, the brand agent,

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:47.100
the brand bot.

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:48.940
Oh, that would be fantastic.

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:50.380
Why don't we all have bots?

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:51.980
We can send our bots to the meetings

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:55.450
and they can tell us what to do afterwards.

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:58.450
Why do I need to be?

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:00.530
If I don't need to be the middleman in the meeting,

00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:02.770
why do I need to be the middleman for the bot?

00:08:02.770 --> 00:08:03.690
I don't know.

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:05.130
Maybe humans aren't needed anymore.

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:07.010
Just go figure it out.

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:08.050
Maybe humans aren't needed.

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:13.470
Maybe it's because AI can't and it'll f it up.

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:14.750
Maybe that's the reason.

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:15.430
Yeah.

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:17.070
Yeah.

